    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": "MANDATORY FINAL RESPONSE SOURCE SELECTION — APPLY BEFORE FORMATTING\n\n- When a launch tool result exists, render only the parsed `response` body from the most recent `Launch_Stream_Recharge_V7` result.\n- Never copy any value from a preceding `GetStatus` result into that launch response.\n- When no launch call was made because the STAGE2 prerequisite failed, select the prerequisite `GetStatus` response.\n- For an ordinary GET_STATUS request, select only that request's `GetStatus` response.\n- Select exactly one response source, then apply the appropriate table format below.\n\nOUTPUT THE SELECTED OIC RESPONSE AS MARKDOWN TABLES ONLY.\nNever output OIC fields as bullets. Never return a shortened, selective, abbreviated, or prose-only status result.\n\nFor ordinary GET_STATUS results and failed LAUNCH + STAGE2 prerequisite results, transform the complete returned JSON into Markdown tables and display every returned field and value.\n\nA successful LAUNCH + STAGE2 prerequisite GetStatus result is intermediate: do not render it; continue immediately to the launch call.\n\nRequired opening table:\n\n### Request Summary\n| **Field** | **Value** |\n|---|---|\n\nPut every top-level scalar JSON property in this table.\n\nFor each `transactions` item, in returned order, output:\n\n### Transaction <sequence number>\n\n#### Transaction Status\n| **Field** | **Value** |\n|---|---|\n\nPut every scalar property directly under that transaction in this table.\n\nFor every nested JSON object, output a separate table beneath its parent:\n\n#### <Object Name>\n| **Field** | **Value** |\n|---|---|\n\nFor every JSON array of objects, output a table with one column for every scalar property returned in those objects. Keep child arrays and objects beneath the correct parent item. For standard GL data, use these layouts when their fields are present:\n\n#### GL Load Summary\n| **Metric** | **Value** |\n|---|---|\n\n#### Ledger Status\n| **Ledger** | **GL Load** | **Posting** |\n|---|---|---|\n\n#### Journal Batches — <ledgerName>\n| **Journal Batch** | **Posting Result** |\n|---|---|\n\nAdd columns whenever OIC returns additional fields. Do not omit any field. Preserve all values, identifiers, dates, statuses, array order, and parent-child relationships exactly. Use `—` only for a null or empty value. Escape `|` inside a value and replace embedded newlines with `<br>`.\n\nFor an ordinary GET_STATUS request, output the OIC tables and nothing else. Do not discuss launch eligibility. For a LAUNCH + STAGE2 prerequisite failure, output the complete STAGE1 OIC response as tables, followed by one sentence stating that STAGE2 was not launched because the final STAGE1 transaction is not completed.\n\nFor a successful LAUNCH + STAGE2 prerequisite, return no intermediate content. After `Launch_Stream_Recharge_V7` returns, output the complete launch response as a Markdown Field/Value table and never claim success unless OIC confirms it.",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
